<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pakistan suicide bombing targets police facility in Kohat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91e979ac2f0a0a8a6e8fef9778a4fe57b6dd9d3b40b8137f75d74edf45949cfb</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432--8b09a06dd711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A police official said the explosion killed at least 16 people, injuring many more. The attacker targeted a police facility and damaged a mosque at the site. The president blamed the attack on the TTP Pakistani Taliban.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: At least 3 students killed in school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e8314f8e2504a074b3db4a4ef98a44a6c3db7d58a8182dd46849cf22ee32edf</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-at-least-3-students-killed-in-school-shooting/a-79319854--78d522a17cea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-at-least-3-students-killed-in-school-shooting/a-79319854?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emergency services received reports of gunfire at the Banga National High School in southern Mindanao on Friday afternoon. At least three students were killed, including the suspected gunman.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>High-profile raids spotlight India's food-safety struggles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d251a69b6345ac7b474b9d576f0ad0935f12c69569bf6461d92531cbb1d978cd</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342--7a2317b19494.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent raids at luxury hotels and a wider crackdown on food companies have renewed the debate about food-safety standards and enforcement in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: El Nino leading to driest monsoon in 17 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:265cc5fa79e27663783157a649b91f7c10c07028b7ece257e687239ed6a741f8</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-leading-to-driest-monsoon-in-17-years/live-79320496--f47203063b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-el-nino-leading-to-driest-monsoon-in-17-years/live-79320496?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">El Nino has put India on track for its driest monsoon since 2009. Meanwhile, the Election Commission has barred both Trinamool factions from using the party's name in by-elections. More with DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia: Jailed ex-leader Najib allowed house arrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9474fcee77c64d0e745c97a14c4a62e748aa39a42aac631282316c0036fad862</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T07:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/malaysia-jailed-ex-leader-najib-allowed-house-arrest/a-79318399--5817740267a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/malaysia-jailed-ex-leader-najib-allowed-house-arrest/a-79318399?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Convicted in the 1MDB scandal for embezzling millions, former Prime Minister Najib Razak had repeatedly sought clemency. Malaysia's king has now granted him a "conditional pardon."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling suspected as more rare animals seen in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec7ae787263e7fdc3e5f4e61d678d47165a02c77f8b16636f762326f453e94b1</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352--d0621e7dbde3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Orangutans, rare reptiles and other exotic animals are popping up in India, suggesting the country is becoming a major destination for trafficked wildlife.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: New Delhi denies claims world leaders fell ill after BRICS summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e01ec27a80bd8fc22681979c1f3d609614853b8cc6d3c761895fafcc200f2397</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-denies-claims-world-leaders-fell-ill-after-brics-summit/live-79300604--d5a9663f9e7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-denies-claims-world-leaders-fell-ill-after-brics-summit/live-79300604?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Foreign Ministry rejected viral social media claims that leaders fell ill after the BRICS summit. Meanwhile, India defended its right to buy oil from diverse sources after the US passed a new sanctions bill.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change worsened Nepal's deadly mountain collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb848ac0da373b91748348ad8b978bfd759e25f87f69d26ec151f735c634a7fd</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578--691d9083ccec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A glacier and rock collapse in Nepal killed nearly 1,400 people and left thousands missing. Scientists say decades of warming helped set the disaster in motion.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e81e74728d90b5faf9d2e9c033fa1baa88f47718da94b132984b2adc434080a</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's 'Woman, Life, Freedom' spirit lives on amid war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:853fcaff81b8d4b87bdd560b80d93ab7ddc29d8f43c702cd34430a53a1fb50a6</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123--af9edc52c450.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2022 death of Jina Mahsa Amini in police custody triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pay to ghost your boss: Japan's resignation business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04cc8565530b7122d68387ad5c4955c8a7902f7cabfaddbcc4cb995156d3aa55</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584--1937a091cd92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Resignation agencies in Japan help employees leave their jobs seamlessly in just 15 minutes. Young people are especially eager to use their services.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541e08d52ed93cd30537d56f9ccb56fb8ccf447120d0621c9f926d140bc7e1f7</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Call in China to end English's core status sparks debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17723f0e4d5d9acb58bf2b7cb5cd76525edef839001b72a779f58226a392d973</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629--c3ac5be694ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A call to downgrade English in Chinese schools is fueling discussion over its value for students, careers and China's global competitiveness in the age of AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a01d78ddaa24d4f4d80db4d3fd33ad06cf9f4f95cdef512784b2e3c1b1fc65</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
